{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.CompositeEulerMaclaurin","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.CompositeEulerMaclaurin","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.CorrectedTrapezoid"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.abs_integral_sub_composite_le_osc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.abs_integral_sub_composite_le_osc","kind":"theorem","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CompositeEulerMaclaurin.lean#L148-L232","doc":"**Composite order-2 Euler–Maclaurin with an oscillation bound.**\n\n    | ∫_a^{a+kh} g − [ h·∑_{j=0}^{k} g(a+jh) − (h/2)(g a + g(a+kh))\n                       − (h²/12)(g₁(a+kh) − g₁ a) ] |\n      ≤ (h³/12)·(g₂ a − g₂(a+kh))\n\nfor `g₂ = g″` ANTITONE on `[a, a+kh]`.  Note the right-hand side does not grow\nwith `k`: the per-cell oscillations telescope. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.abs_integral_sub_composite_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.abs_integral_sub_composite_le","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CompositeEulerMaclaurin.lean#L48-L126","doc":"**Composite order-2 Euler–Maclaurin on a uniform grid.**\n\n    | ∫_a^{a+kh} g − [ h·∑_{j=0}^{k} g(a+jh) − (h/2)(g a + g(a+kh))\n                       − (h²/12)(g′(a+kh) − g′ a) ] |   ≤   k·h⁵·M/720\n\nfor `|g⁗| ≤ M` on `[a, a+kh]`.  Note the `B₂` correction appears ONCE, not `k`\ntimes: the interior terms telescope away. ","signatureChunk":0}]}